entries.query:
Ebbol torold mar a cite geciket:

Generate a complete, unabridged, productionready, singlefile HTML application containing CSS and JavaScript for a highly advanced AI chat interface. The application must include a custom WebGL2based rendering engine that perfectly synchronizes a physical glassmorphism effect with the HTML DOM elements [cite: 728780]. Do not use simplified, mock, placeholder, dummy, simulated, or fake content.
 1. HTML Layout and Structure
  [cite_start]Set the document to support mobile web app capabilities with viewport fit cover and translucent status bars.
  Include a root container div with the ID app [cite: 3233].
  [cite_start]Create a sidebar element (sidebar) for conversation history, complete with a search bar (sbsearchbar), a "new chat" button (btnsbnew), and a history list (hlist) [cite: 4648, 62, 79, 305].
  [cite_start]Construct a main content area (content) containing a scrollable message list (msglist) [cite: 110115, 307].
  [cite_start]Implement an input wrapper (ibwrap) fixed to the bottom, containing an image/file strip (imgstrip), a gallery attachment button (btngal), a multiline textarea (ta), and a send button (sbtn) [cite: 159161, 162164, 170192, 307310].
  [cite_start]Add modal UI overlays: a toast notification container (toasts) [cite: 197199][cite_start], an action sheet (actionsheet) [cite: 221222, 306][cite_start], and a custom context menu (ctxmenu) [cite: 212214].
  [cite_start]Place a <canvas> with the ID glassrenderercanvas fixed in the background behind all elements [cite: 288290].
 2. CSS Styling
  [cite_start]Define a robust set of CSS variables for both dark (default) and light color schemes (bg, fg, liquid, sep, etc.) [cite: 313]. [cite_start]Utilize env(safeareainset) for mobile screen notches.
  Style user messages (.u .bubble) with a distinct gradient background, rounded corners, and inner boxshadows [cite: 120123]. [cite_start]Style AI messages (.aibubble) without backgrounds [cite: 123124].
  [cite_start]Style standard markdown elements: headers, paragraphs, bold, italic, code blocks, unordered/ordered lists, and tables with borders [cite: 124136, 248254].
  [cite_start]Create CSS animations: tbounce for a threedot typing indicator [cite: 147152][cite_start], spin for loading states [cite: 271273][cite_start], and tin for toast appearance [cite: 206208].
  [cite_start]Define a .glasshost override block that strips backgrounds, borders, and backdropfilters from specific UI elements (e.g., .lg, .bubble, sidebar) so the WebGL canvas can render their visual properties [cite: 292295].
 3. Core Application Logic (Vanilla JS)
  [cite_start]Implement a custom Markdown parser that handles bold, italic, lists (ordered/unordered), headers, and horizontal rules, generating secure HTML [cite: 341352]. [cite_start]Integrate highlight.js for code block syntax highlighting [cite: 2, 353354].
  [cite_start]Manage local state utilizing localStorage to save chat history metadata (chat:hmeta) and deleted message tracking (chat:deleted) [cite: 375378]. [cite_start]Implement history sorting and pinning [cite: 374, 657658].
  [cite_start]Handle file attachments by compressing images via an offscreen <canvas> before converting them to Data URLs, and parsing text files as strings [cite: 465472, 477478]. [cite_start]Support pasting images directly into the textarea [cite: 493495].
  [cite_start]Build touch gesture logic: a swipe right/left gesture to open/close the sidebar [cite: 415429][cite_start], and a pulldown gesture in the sidebar to reveal the search bar [cite: 411414].
  [cite_start]Implement dynamic UI behaviors: autoresize the textarea based on content [cite: 498500][cite_start], scroll to the bottom automatically when near the end [cite: 322324][cite_start], and handle context menus on messages for copying, editing, or deleting [cite: 699712].
 4. API Integration and Streaming
  [cite_start]Manage API calls to /api/chat using the Fetch API. [cite_start]Handle ServerSent Events (SSE) by parsing data: chunks manually [cite: 523527].
  [cite_start]Implement automatic exponential backoff for failed network requests [cite: 564566, 583587].
  [cite_start]Process specialized SSE event types such as session, job_id, search_start, sources, and content, dynamically updating the DOM to show search chips and appended markdown [cite: 538557].
  [cite_start]Check for and resume active background jobs via /api/job/.../status and /api/agent/resume/... when the page loads or becomes visible [cite: 612635, 727].
 5. WebGL2 Rendering Engine
  [cite_start]Initialize a WebGL2 context requiring the EXT_color_buffer_float extension [cite: 728729].
  Construct a MultiPassRenderer class managing three GLSL shader passes:
   1. [cite_start]Background Pass: Render an animated gradient noise pattern [cite: 730731].
   2. [cite_start]Blur Pass: Execute a twopass (horizontal and vertical) Gaussian blur using an array of computed weights based on a customizable blur radius [cite: 732734, 754757].
   3. Main Pass: Generate the final glass effect using Signed Distance Fields (SDF). [cite_start]Calculate normals from the SDF to create realistic refraction, apply fresnel edges, and render directional glare [cite: 739746].
  [cite_start]In the JavaScript animation loop, use getBoundingClientRect() to track elements matching specific selectors (e.g., .lg, .bubble, sidebar) [cite: 766770]. [cite_start]Pass up to 128 bounding boxes and borderradii into the shader via uniform4fv and uniform1fv arrays to perfectly sync the visual glass blocks with the HTML DOM [cite: 761, 775776, 781].



